---
// PRD 7.6: a short first-person note, left-aligned, with a small signature wordmark. It carries the
// page's one dealt moment (taste-skill word-highlight): the statement rests at half ink and turns to
// ink word by word as it crosses the middle of the screen, "the whole point" to the accent.
// Reduced motion and no script: the statement in full ink.
---

<section class="section note" id="studio" data-moment="word-highlight" aria-label="A note from the studio" style="--h: 1">
  <div class="wrap">
    <!-- a p, as the kit's moment expects. Its script adds an aria-label to it, which Lighthouse flags
         on a paragraph (accessibility 96); as an h2 the taste gate fails it as a run-on heading. -->
    <p class="mo-wh__text note__text">
      I build these apps in the evenings, one at a time. Each starts with something I wanted fixed in my
      own week, and stays small on purpose. If one helps you, that's <strong>the whole point</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="note__sign"><span class="wordmark">victoir</span> Vijay Kumar</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .note .wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    align-content: start;
  }
  /* the moment's own CSS sets the face; this sets the size for a statement that fills its screen */
  .note .note__text {
    font-size: clamp(2.125rem, 1.4rem + 2.9vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    max-width: 1000px;
  }
  .note__sign {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .note__sign .wordmark {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
